<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Inpatient & Ward Management</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Manage complex inpatient care pathways with architectural precision, ensuring patient 
            safety through structured clinical handovers and real-time ward visibility.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Dynamic Bed & Ward Allocation</h2>
        <p>
            Gain absolute visibility of your facility's capacity through a live 'Bed Map'. 
            Admissions staff can assign patients to specific beds across departments—General 
            Wards, Private Suites, Maternity, and Pediatric units. The system tracks 
            bed status (Occupied, To-be-cleaned, Maintenance) in real-time, optimizing 
            turnaround times and ensuring that the right patient is always in the right 
            care environment.
        </p>
        <p>
            Internal transfers between wards (e.g., from HDU to General Ward) are managed 
            through a structured workflow, maintaining the continuity of the 
            clinical record throughout the patient's stay.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Digital Nursing & Bedside Care</h2>
        <p>
            Standardize institutional care with digital nursing observation charts. Nurses 
            capture hourly vitals, medication administration records (eMAR), and 
            fluid balance charts directly at the bedside. The system provides 
            automated alerts for overdue observations or deteriorating vital signs, 
            empowering nursing teams to escalate care proactively.
        </p>
        <p>
            Ward round documentation and doctor's orders—for medications, lab investigations, 
            or wound care—are instantly visible to the nursing team, ensuring that care 
            plans are executed exactly as prescribed by the clinical leadership.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Structured Discharge Orchestration</h2>
        <p>
            The discharge process is a critical moment for patient safety. Pindah Health 
            manages the entire discharge workflow—from the final clinician sign-off 
            to the generation of professional Discharge Summaries. These summaries 
            automatically include diagnosis codes, medication history during stay, 
            follow-up instructions, and simplified patient-education materials.
        </p>
        <p>
            Coordination with the Pharmacy for 'Take Home' (TTO) medications and with the 
            Billing department for final account reconciliation ensures a smooth 
            and professional exit for every patient.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

